{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540664-how-much-is-the-umbra-dependent-on-humans","id":1540664,"title":"how much is the umbra dependent on humans?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-18T16:28:45-07:00","id":1540664,"title":"how much is the umbra dependent on humans?","content":"how much does human thought affect umbra? there are places and things in the umbra that contradict the idea that reality is wholly shaped by humanity (i.e. the deep umbra and the aliens) is it only earth and the moon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27683-bernese","name":"Bernese","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T16:47:30-07:00","id":1540666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bernese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540664-how-much-is-the-umbra-dependent-on-humans#post1540664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how much does human thought affect umbra? there are places and things in the umbra that contradict the idea that reality is wholly shaped by humanity (i.e. the deep umbra and the aliens) is it only earth and the moon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m pretty sure the Near Umbra includes Earth and the Moon. The Far Umbra includes the other eight planets of the solar system (including the Shard Realms and the Shade Realms) and the Deep Umbra is everything beyond the solar system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T16:49:31-07:00","id":1540667,"title":"","content":"The idea that reality is <i>wholly </i>shaped by humanity doesn't even stand up to scrutiny on <i>Earth</i>. There are Earthly Foundations that serve as a baseline of reality that the Consensus cannot change, for example. <br /> <br /> I'm not surprised that the Umbra tends to be free of human meddling. <br /> <br /> My own view on it is that the Gauntlet shields the Umbra from the effects of the Consensus. And the Umbra itself has a second layer of defense in that humans who migrate to the Umbra tend to turn into spirits, losing their Avatars (Awake or Asleep) in the process. So the Umbra <i>proper</i>, as opposed to Umbral Realms that have their own form of Gauntlet between them and the Umbra itself, is unlikely to ever be colonized by humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T18:28:02-07:00","id":1540675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bernese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540664-how-much-is-the-umbra-dependent-on-humans#post1540664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how much does human thought affect umbra? there are places and things in the umbra that contradict the idea that reality is wholly shaped by humanity (i.e. the deep umbra and the aliens) is it only earth and the moon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, even the Penumbra is barely affected by human thought, it mostly reflects stationary fixtures plus natural &quot;energies&quot;. Heck, as far as we can see, the Umbra is more dominated by plants than by anything else.<br /> <br /> The Middle Umbra has almost no human influence. The Astral Umbra is made of thoughts, but it's easy to imagine that we mostly see it reflecting human thoughts because they're more comprehensible for us, and comprehension is key in the Astral. Otherwise it's made of the thoughts of everything that thinks in some manner, and we simply don't know what that may be.<br /> <br /> Only the Low Umbra seems to be human-centric, but the Low Umbra is another can of worms entirely.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear: IIRC the Near Umbra covers Earth, Moon, Mars and the Asteroid Belt. Beyond the Near Umbra and as far as we know, there's no Gauntlet, so matter and spirit are together, which isn't the same as to say the planets don't exist as concrete entities. We may be the center of the universe or not, it can't be made certain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T06:49:27-07:00","id":1540701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540664-how-much-is-the-umbra-dependent-on-humans?p=1540667#post1540667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that reality is <i>wholly </i>shaped by humanity doesn't even stand up to scrutiny on <i>Earth</i>. There are Earthly Foundations that serve as a baseline of reality that the Consensus cannot change, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good baseline position, but I should point out that we have come up with ways that the Consensus could work where it really does wholly (or nearly wholly) shape all of reality. Also, what does and does not constitute an Earthly Foundation and how strong they are is up in the air. So its not so much that it doesn't pass scrutiny, its that no simple explanation works and most games have no need for a complicated one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My own view on it is that the Gauntlet shields the Umbra from the effects of the Consensus. And the Umbra itself has a second layer of defense in that humans who migrate to the Umbra tend to turn into spirits, losing their Avatars (Awake or Asleep) in the process. So the Umbra <i>proper</i>, as opposed to Umbral Realms that have their own form of Gauntlet between them and the Umbra itself, is unlikely to ever be colonized by humans. </div> </div> </div>I've grown to like the 2nd edition idea that spirits themselves have an impact on the Consensus. It is a surprisingly clever idea that gives the Consensus inertia. Spirits relate to how the world is now, so they reinforce the current Consensus and push against changes. However, if the world does change, the spirits slowly change to match (because they aren't changed by the Consensus, they are changed because they reflect the world), eventually reinforcing rather than opposing the new normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T10:56:05-07:00","id":1540716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540664-how-much-is-the-umbra-dependent-on-humans?p=1540701#post1540701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a good baseline position, but I should point out that we have come up with ways that the Consensus could work where it really does wholly (or nearly wholly) shape all of reality. Also, what does and does not constitute an Earthly Foundation and how strong they are is up in the air. So its not so much that it doesn't pass scrutiny, its that no simple explanation works and most games have no need for a complicated one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I've grown to like the 2nd edition idea that spirits themselves have an impact on the Consensus. It is a surprisingly clever idea that gives the Consensus inertia. Spirits relate to how the world is now, so they reinforce the current Consensus and push against changes. However, if the world does change, the spirits slowly change to match (because they aren't changed by the Consensus, they are changed because they reflect the world), eventually reinforcing rather than opposing the new normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. To me, the world of Mage is Subjective - FULLY Subjective. There's really no room for a middle ground here, because either the Moon exists irregardless of my solipsism, or the Moon exists only when I'm looking at it because I expect it to be there.<br /> <br /> Now, sure, the Earth's tides don't rely on my fishing schedule alone (or does it now?), which is why this fabulous thing called &quot;reality&quot; is built based on a CONSENSUS.<br /> <br /> But a Consensus of what exactly?<br /> <br /> And 2nd ed gave this possibility, and indeed it makes sense, that humans are not the only ones - and probably, not even the most relevant ones - agents of Consensus.<br /> <br /> AKA if you want to change gravity, first you'll have to ask permission for all spirits to change their minds.<br /> <br /> All of WoD has heavy Gnostic ideas, with the 2 major offenders being Mage and Demon the Fall. This idea of subjective reality comes straight out from gnosticism. Mage also has the idea of &quot;the One&quot; and of &quot;Avatars&quot; as &quot;shards of the One&quot;. This is Gnosticism 101. In fact, &quot;we are all God&quot;, everything you see and hear and feel around you is also God, and essentially all the &quot;reality&quot; is just God having a drug induced &quot;bad trip&quot; crazy dream. &quot;Ascension&quot;, the most Gnostic thing I have ever seen, is reaching unity with &quot;the One&quot; or with &quot;the Whole&quot;, finally realizing that everything is in fact the same thing (God).<br /> <br /> Therefore, a &quot;gravity spirit&quot; which &quot;believes things should always fall down&quot; is constantly reinforcing the &quot;Consensus of Gravity&quot;. Mages call this &quot;Earthly Foundation&quot; simply because there's too many spirits reinforcing that idea, so much so that the whole of humanity wouldn't be able to change it.<br /> <br /> But, since me, you, gravity spirits, rocks and plants and the dirty beneath our feet and the air above our heads, since that all is actually the same thing and that thing is &quot;God&quot;, then that simply means that &quot;God&quot; is much more stubborn about gravity in his drug induced dream where the almighty thinks he is an infinitude of things (rather than the single one all encompassing cosmic unity), than he is about which kinds of magic should be coincidental or vulgar. There are many many more pieces of God dreaming about gravity than there are pieces dreaming about a day where cellphones will no longer work.<br /> <br /> Therefore, I wouldn't say that &quot;Consensus&quot; or &quot;Earthly Foundations&quot; are things 'set on stone', funnily enough. Things (probably) are more complicated than they seem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T11:31:57-07:00","id":1540718,"title":"","content":"Allow me to clarify something here that seems to be getting lost: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bernese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540664-how-much-is-the-umbra-dependent-on-humans#post1540664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how much does <span style=\"color:#e74c3c\">human</span> thought affect umbra? there are places and things in the umbra that contradict the idea that reality is wholly shaped <span style=\"color:#e74c3c\">by humanity</span> (i.e. the deep umbra and the aliens) is it only earth and the moon?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540664-how-much-is-the-umbra-dependent-on-humans?p=1540667#post1540667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that reality is <i>wholly </i>shaped <span style=\"color:#e74c3c\">by humanity</span> doesn't even stand up to scrutiny on <i>Earth</i>. There are Earthly Foundations that serve as a baseline of reality that the Consensus cannot change, for example.<br /> <br /> I'm not surprised that the Umbra tends to be free of <span style=\"color:#e74c3c\">human</span> meddling.<br /> <br /> My own view on it is that the Gauntlet shields the Umbra from the effects of the Consensus. And the Umbra itself has a second layer of defense in that <span style=\"color:#e74c3c\">humans</span> who migrate to the Umbra tend to turn into spirits, losing their Avatars (Awake or Asleep) in the process. So the Umbra <i>proper</i>, as opposed to Umbral Realms that have their own form of Gauntlet between them and the Umbra itself, is unlikely to ever be colonized <span style=\"color:#e74c3c\">by humans</span>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question asked, and my initial response, were both about humanity's influence on reality. Is it possible that reality in <b>Mage</b> is wholly subjective, but that there are more participants in defining that subjectivity than just humans? Sure! While I won't go so far as to say that Mages reality <i>is</i> 100% subjective, I have no problem saying that that's a possibility. <br /> <br /> But again, the original assertion wasn't that reality isn't wholly subjective; it was that it isn't wholly shaped by human beliefs. And there's no doubt about that. Maybe I should have said &quot;the human Consensus&quot; instead of &quot;the Consensus&quot; in my post in order to be more clear; but in my defense, the books always use &quot;the Consensus&quot; to refer to collective human beliefs. <br /> <br /> Is the larger reality determined only by beliefs, with a larger Consensus that includes gods and monsters as well as humans? It's possible. But there <i>are</i> some things that the Consensus has little to no say over, and it doesn't matter if that's because they're fundamental truths or because God said so. The practical effects are the same. <br /> <br /> And since there seems to be a tendency to jump to assumptions here, let me clarify one other thing: Earthly Foundations aren't absolute. They <i>can</i> be overruled \u2014 by individuals, no less; because in Mage, an individual Awakened is more capable of effecting change than the entire Consensus is. The Consensus cannot overrule Earthly Foundations; a Mage absolutely <i>can. </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T19:18:23-07:00","id":1540741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540664-how-much-is-the-umbra-dependent-on-humans?p=1540718#post1540718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> And since there seems to be a tendency to jump to assumptions here, let me clarify one other thing: Earthly Foundations aren't absolute. They <i>can</i> be overruled \u2014 by individuals, no less; because in Mage, an individual Awakened is more capable of effecting change than the entire Consensus is. The Consensus cannot overrule Earthly Foundations; a Mage absolutely <i>can. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>The eternal problems is that no earthly foundation is ever given. <br /> <br /> The only exemple of some sort of unchangeable truths, such as the need for an avatar to be a mage, the existence of the spirit world regardless of the efforts of the technocracy and so on, are beyond the abilities of mage to twist, so they hardly match the concept of earthly foundations. <br /> <br /> In the end, the only thing that seems to match is that reality don't like rewinding time. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T06:41:05-07:00","id":1540762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The eternal problems is that no earthly foundation is ever given. </div> </div> </div>This is objectively false:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Some things are almost always vulgar, no matter <i>who's</i> doing them, <i>where</i> they're doing them, or <i>how</i> they're being done. In game terms, acts that vulgar these Earthly Foundations contradict the baseline reality for Earth. </span></div><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Sudden Large Alterations of Physical and Metaphysical Mass or Space: \u2026</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Obvious violations of normal physical laws: \u2026</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Cross- dimensional rifts: \u2026</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Messing with the time stream: \u2026</span></li> </ul><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">M20 pp.612\u2013613</div> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> There you go: four Earthly Foundations given in M20, specifically right where the concept of Earthly Foundations are first presented. There are caveats in there (e.g., &quot;almost always vulgar&quot;), and you might disagree with one or two of the examples given (which, given Storyteller's prerogative, means that they're not Earthly Foundations in <i>your </i>games); but that doesn't change the fact that four examples of Earthly Foundations <i>are</i> given.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Fixed weird bug 08-20-2024, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T08:00:31-07:00","id":1540771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Astral Umbra is made of thoughts, but it's easy to imagine that we mostly see it reflecting human thoughts because they're more comprehensible for us, and comprehension is key in the Astral. Otherwise it's made of the thoughts of everything that thinks in some manner, and we simply don't know what that may be.<br /> <br /> Only the Low Umbra seems to be human-centric, but the Low Umbra is another can of worms entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say the Astral Umbra it's more human-centric than the Low.<br /> <br /> Nearly everything we know about the Astral it's made of very &quot;human&quot;, like the whole layers based on religion, science &amp; language. It's spirits are very aware of human culture and deeply care about it. It's also the place that was affected the most by the Avatar Storm, and it's the place on the Umbra that's most related to Avatars as these apparelty go to the Cave before reincarnating.<br /> <br /> Theorizing that &quot;everything that thinks in some manner&quot; builds the Astral Umbra up, and that thus there should be a lot more to it &quot;and we simply don't know what that may be&quot; because it's outside of our perception, it's interesting, and very plausible given what we know about the Astral, but the opperative words here it's &quot;<b>we simply don't know</b>&quot;, becuse there's no concrete evidence anywhere that that's the case.<br /> <br /> Like I could equally posit that there's another Low Umbra we know nothing about, that's made for Dogs, and that we can't perceive because it's not out afterlife.<br /> <br /> At the very east, the Low Umbra has huge swats of chaos and eldrich horrors, that seem to have little to nothing to do with humanity. Humanity it's the only thing that seems to <i>create stuff </i>there, but I wouldn't say it's <i>dependant </i>on humanity, it just would be a lot emptier w/o us.<br /> <br /> In comparison, there's very little, if anything, about the geography of the Astral that can't be linked with humans in some way, thus I think it's the one layer one could trully say to be <i>dependant</i> on humanity w/o anything breaking, AFAIK. It could be reasonable for it to just vanish if humanity it's gone\u200b <hr /><br /> Personally, I'm of the theory that the Astral has a relationship of <i>co-dependence </i>with (human?) tought. It's very clear that human tought shapes and creates the Umbra, when you have stuff like rivers made of the history of languages, but at the same time the deepths of the Astral represents concepts so important to tought that, in a Kantian way, we could speak of an &quot;a priory&quot; of sorts: that w/o the Astral humans <i>wouldn't be able to think.</i><br /> <br /> My theory it's that the most powerful entities of the Astral, the rearely mentioned Uthra (Celestine level Astral entities), and the deepest layers, are so integral to our tought that asking who depends on who could be a bit of a chicken and egg thing.<br /> <br /> And I think that's very pliable to the idea that the Astral could be made/make &quot;the thoughts of everything that thinks&quot;. Primeval concepts such as Emptyness are shared by multplie sp\u00e8cies and could &quot;rule-be ruled&quot; by multiple entities rather than just humanity.<br /> <br /> BUT, that's just a theory. <hr /><br /> Albeit the Astral and the Low are the only layers where the influence it's massive, &quot;humanity&quot; migth be said to influence other places:<br /> <br /> Probably the strongest, albeit not the only, example it's the Cyberrealm on the Middle Umbra: it's deeply influenced by human activity to the point it changes shape according to human technology. Now, I wouldn't say that this influence has anything to do with the <i>Consensus</i>, but it's a good example of how human influence it's not just about &quot;Belief&quot;. &quot;Actions&quot; also shape the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-20-2024, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T13:03:12-07:00","id":1540852,"title":"","content":"Uthra (Celestine level Astral entities)<br /> <br /> which book are these beings mentioned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27683-bernese","name":"Bernese","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T14:37:47-07:00","id":1540856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540664-how-much-is-the-umbra-dependent-on-humans?p=1540718#post1540718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allow me to clarify something here that seems to be getting lost:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The question asked, and my initial response, were both about humanity's influence on reality. Is it possible that reality in <b>Mage</b> is wholly subjective, but that there are more participants in defining that subjectivity than just humans? Sure! While I won't go so far as to say that Mages reality <i>is</i> 100% subjective, I have no problem saying that that's a possibility.<br /> <br /> But again, the original assertion wasn't that reality isn't wholly subjective; it was that it isn't wholly shaped by human beliefs. And there's no doubt about that. Maybe I should have said &quot;the human Consensus&quot; instead of &quot;the Consensus&quot; in my post in order to be more clear; but in my defense, the books always use &quot;the Consensus&quot; to refer to collective human beliefs.<br /> <br /> Is the larger reality determined only by beliefs, with a larger Consensus that includes gods and monsters as well as humans? It's possible. But there <i>are</i> some things that the Consensus has little to no say over, and it doesn't matter if that's because they're fundamental truths or because God said so. The practical effects are the same.<br /> <br /> And since there seems to be a tendency to jump to assumptions here, let me clarify one other thing: Earthly Foundations aren't absolute. They <i>can</i> be overruled \u2014 by individuals, no less; because in Mage, an individual Awakened is more capable of effecting change than the entire Consensus is. The Consensus cannot overrule Earthly Foundations; a Mage absolutely <i>can. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I wasn't disputing that. I just wanted to show some more light about what exactly is &quot;Consensus&quot;. Whatever the case, &quot;Human Consensus&quot; is obviously just a small piece of the broader &quot;Consensus&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T14:57:04-07:00","id":1540857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540664-how-much-is-the-umbra-dependent-on-humans?p=1540771#post1540771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say the Astral Umbra it's more human-centric than the Low.<br /> <br /> Nearly everything we know about the Astral it's made of very &quot;human&quot;, like the whole layers based on religion, science &amp; language. It's spirits are very aware of human culture and deeply care about it. It's also the place that was affected the most by the Avatar Storm, and it's the place on the Umbra that's most related to Avatars as these apparelty go to the Cave before reincarnating.<br /> <br /> Theorizing that &quot;everything that thinks in some manner&quot; builds the Astral Umbra up, and that thus there should be a lot more to it &quot;and we simply don't know what that may be&quot; because it's outside of our perception, it's interesting, and very plausible given what we know about the Astral, but the opperative words here it's &quot;<b>we simply don't know</b>&quot;, becuse there's no concrete evidence anywhere that that's the case.<br /> <br /> Like I could equally posit that there's another Low Umbra we know nothing about, that's made for Dogs, and that we can't perceive because it's not out afterlife.<br /> <br /> At the very east, the Low Umbra has huge swats of chaos and eldrich horrors, that seem to have little to nothing to do with humanity. Humanity it's the only thing that seems to <i>create stuff </i>there, but I wouldn't say it's <i>dependant </i>on humanity, it just would be a lot emptier w/o us.<br /> <br /> In comparison, there's very little, if anything, about the geography of the Astral that can't be linked with humans in some way, thus I think it's the one layer one could trully say to be <i>dependant</i> on humanity w/o anything breaking, AFAIK. It could be reasonable for it to just vanish if humanity it's gone <hr /><br /> Personally, I'm of the theory that the Astral has a relationship of <i>co-dependence </i>with (human?) tought. It's very clear that human tought shapes and creates the Umbra, when you have stuff like rivers made of the history of languages, but at the same time the deepths of the Astral represents concepts so important to tought that, in a Kantian way, we could speak of an &quot;a priory&quot; of sorts: that w/o the Astral humans <i>wouldn't be able to think.</i><br /> <br /> My theory it's that the most powerful entities of the Astral, the rearely mentioned Uthra (Celestine level Astral entities), and the deepest layers, are so integral to our tought that asking who depends on who could be a bit of a chicken and egg thing.<br /> <br /> And I think that's very pliable to the idea that the Astral could be made/make &quot;the thoughts of everything that thinks&quot;. Primeval concepts such as Emptyness are shared by multplie sp\u00e8cies and could &quot;rule-be ruled&quot; by multiple entities rather than just humanity.<br /> <br /> BUT, that's just a theory. <hr /><br /> Albeit the Astral and the Low are the only layers where the influence it's massive, &quot;humanity&quot; migth be said to influence other places:<br /> <br /> Probably the strongest, albeit not the only, example it's the Cyberrealm on the Middle Umbra: it's deeply influenced by human activity to the point it changes shape according to human technology. Now, I wouldn't say that this influence has anything to do with the <i>Consensus</i>, but it's a good example of how human influence it's not just about &quot;Belief&quot;. &quot;Actions&quot; also shape the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually interesting. It could well be that all thoughts humans (and perhaps the thoughts of all animistic entities that exist everywhere and in everything) are actually just manifestations of the Astral Plane. And that human languages don't manifest in the Astral Plane, but rather that humans access the languages fluctuating in the ether of the Astral Plane.<br /> <br /> It is indeed impossible to stablish which is dependent on what. And mayhaps, thinking minds and the Astral Plane form a closed system of interdependency, upon which one is not possible without the other.<br /> <br /> As for the Eldritch horrors of the Low Umbra, I'm not so sure that those are completely independent from &quot;human&quot; (or other minds) perceptions. Those Eldritch things could be things from the subconscious. Anyone that has ever enjoyed a nightmare (and I love when I have a nightmare, I'm not kidding, I really do, I delight the horrific surreal experience of nightmares) have similar surreal landscapes.<br /> <br /> Many of the things of the Low Umbra reassemble the Dreaming more than anything.<br /> <br /> However, the Oblivion and the Neverborn may still be beyond that, so yeah, it could be that at least something in it are &quot;Earthly Foundations&quot; not connected to &quot;Human Consensus&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T17:44:10-07:00","id":1540865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540664-how-much-is-the-umbra-dependent-on-humans?p=1540771#post1540771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of cool stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, it's a conundrum that can be tackled from multiple angles, and still end up in the same answer: it's unknown, and possibly unknowable.<br /> <br /> The Middle Umbra rests as a very good (if not definitive) proof that humans aren't needed for the Umbrae to exist. The others we only know through a thoroughly human perspective, but while it can be evidence of them being dependant on us, we can't really posit it with any certainty.<br /> <br /> In fact, the only way to be more or less sure would be to find evidence of the opposite, by finding truly inhuman phenomena within them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T11:50:17-07:00","id":1541072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bernese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1540664-how-much-is-the-umbra-dependent-on-humans?p=1540852#post1540852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uthra (Celestine level Astral entities)<br /> <br /> which book are these beings mentioned?</div> </div> </div> </div>Book of Madness 1e, p 122-123. and I think it was never mentioned again. It's a a book packed with obscure, lost and/or deprecated &quot;take with a grain of salt&quot;, pieces of Lore that I nevertheless like a lot. I like it more than the &quot;newer&quot; edition that focuses solely on mages (Marauder, Nephandi)<br /> <br /> Quoting the relevant part:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Uthra or Celestines</b><br /> These are, quite literally, gods. They are revered (though not worshipped) by the Celestial Chorus as beings closer to the One than humans. It's said that they're the very first thoughts of the Creator at the Dawn of the Tellurian, evolved into powerful and complex beings over time, yet still retaining their purity. Some mages believe they are some of the very first shards of the Pure Ones, greater and more pure than the splinters humanity possesses<br /> Some call such beings Celestines, ranging in power from the Great Triad of Garou cosmology to the old gods of humanity's past. Others label them Uthra, intellectual concepts rather than natural ones... </div> </div> </div>Uthra would be a Celestine seen through an &quot;intelectual lense&quot;. altrough this concept of Celestine it's vaguer than what we use since it includes things that aren't. Updated to the M20 lore about Umbral Beings, they're probably equivalent to the concept of &quot;Godhead&quot;<br /> <br /> In any case. It kinda makes sense for there to be such beings ruling the Astral Umbra, because the superior Archangels the Hermetics know about are very consistently presented as Incarna-level entities (like Gabriel on the Book of Worlds). If there's Astral Incarna, there could be higher powers above them. And it makes sense for there to be greater entities above the Archangels","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}